{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490210,"nonce":"JRDtH4//CgHdkPKyPTX4YPbpZl4=","title":"Format GIC documents","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nProvide deterministic browser-neutral GIC formatting and expose it through Monaco's Format Document action. Establish the setting and adapter contract later used by explicit file saving for format-on-save.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Valid representative programs receive canonical formatting without changing parsed meaning.\n- [ ] Formatting is idempotent.\n- [ ] Incomplete or invalid source has documented safe behavior and never corrupts the editor buffer.\n- [ ] Monaco's Format Document action applies the shared formatter result.\n- [ ] A persisted format-on-save setting exists, is enabled by default, and is configurable.\n- [ ] The formatter and setting contract use no Monaco, filesystem, desktop, or LSP types.\n- [ ] Service tests and Playwright acceptance cover formatting and the setting UI.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- git-bug issue `184f8de` — Replace the browser textarea with Monaco","files":null}]}